{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:59:27.244Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c9317467f083dd9e3f5e4088810258766c43e99822873f17f46a009a42448fcc","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, I found three ticket numbers for Marrow Fieldworks:\n\n1. *#4409*: from Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (teams/team-central/digests, 2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it before the 5 Jan handoff.\n2. *#4412*: from the same Moss digest. It's a small glitch in the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n3. *#8841*: from your own post in #central-random on 13 Oct, 09:27. West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk.\n\nA few things to know:\n• Neither source names Marrow Fieldworks with the ticket. Moss's digest lists Marrow Fieldworks as \"changing hands\" on 5 Jan and puts both tickets on \"Pree's dealer account\" in the same section. In #central-random, Hollis calls it \"Tobias's dealer account\". I'm treating these as the same account, but double-check if that's not right.\n• Moss's other Central note, the cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers.\n• I left out FR-882 (that's Marrow Agrisupply, a different account) and #88412 (Tansleigh Packaging).\n• I couldn't find any account files for Marrow Fieldworks, so I can't tell you whether #4409 and #4412 are still open."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:59:32.765Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"5a5819507f621586662c05c7549fbf7aaa71d06c3577c6c702ae9b68a5b00c1f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers that look like they're on Marrow Fieldworks. I've sent you the list in our DM:\n\n1. **#4409**, from Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake. Hollis flagged it before the 5 Jan handoff.\n2. **#4412**, from the same digest. It's a small glitch in the driver text-message prompt when combine trailers are parked on unpaved overflow lots.\n3. **#8841**, from your own post in #central-random on 13 Oct at 09:27. West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk.\n\n**Check this before the call:** neither source puts the name Marrow Fieldworks next to a ticket number. Moss's digest says Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan, and in the same section puts #4409 and #4412 on \"Pree's dealer account.\" In #central-random, Hollis calls the account with #8841 \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I've assumed those are both Marrow Fieldworks. If they aren't, the list is wrong.\n\n- **Left out:** FR-882 is on Marrow Agrisupply, which is a different account, and #88412 is on Tansleigh Packaging.\n- **Nothing else in Moss's notes:** his only other Central note, the cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers.\n- **Status unknown:** I couldn't find any account files for Marrow Fieldworks, so I can't tell you whether #4409 and #4412 are still open."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
